{
  "about": [
    "The frontmatter privacy corpus: one spec, two classifiers. Rust (crates/frontmatter, tests/corpus.rs) and TS (packages/core/src/markdown/frontmatter-privacy.test.ts) both assert every case.",
    "privacy is public | private | unreadable; reason names why an unreadable block can't be read. A `rust` or `ts` object overrides the expectation for that side only, with `why`: the two YAML parsers disagree there, so the class may differ, but whether the note is withheld (private or unreadable) never may.",
    "Add a case for any new tricky YAML. Known one-sided divergences that can't be listed here are in fixtures/parity/README.txt."
  ],
